course: dictionary
lesson: 8293
title: What is a rite?
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A rite is a ceremony that is done in a fixed way, the same each time, often for religious or serious reasons. «At a Hindu funeral the body is usually cremated; traditionally the eldest son leads the rites.» The clue words are funeral, ceremony and leads: rites are the set actions people carry out at an important time.
explain: The words around a word give you clues. This sentence is about a funeral, so rites must be the serious ceremony and the actions done during it. Check by swapping in your meaning: "the ceremonies are led by the eldest son" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: A rite of passage is an event that marks a big change in your life, like losing your first tooth or starting secondary school. You move from one stage of life to the next, and everyone goes through it.
explain: Rite sounds the same as write, right and wright, but the meanings are different. Write means to put down words, right means correct, and wright means a maker, as in playwright. Only rite means a ceremony.
fact: A rite is a ceremony that is done in a fixed way, the same each time.
fact: Religious rites include baptism, weddings and funerals.
fact: A rite of passage marks a big change in someone's life, like becoming an adult.
fact: Rite, write, right and wright all sound the same but have different meanings.
fact: «Rites» means more than one ceremony; «rite» means a single ceremony.
exercise: «At a Hindu funeral the body is usually cremated; traditionally the eldest son leads the rites.» What are the rites? | Clothes worn by the family | *Ceremonies done in a fixed way | Songs sung on birthdays | Fires used for cooking
exercise: Which word means a religious or serious ceremony? | *rite | right | wrong | write
exercise: Losing your first tooth can be called a rite of passage. Why? | It only happens to adults | *It marks a big change that everyone goes through | Teeth are very small | It is a kind of school test
test: Which word means a religious or serious ceremony? | *rite | right | wright | write
test: A playwright is a maker of plays. Which word from the same sound-alike group means a maker? | right | rite | *wright | write
exam: What does «the last rites» most likely mean? | Final repairs to a shoe | The last words on a test | *Ceremonies given to someone who is dying | Running late for the bus
